'''Nafi''', also known as '''Sirak''', is an [[Austronesian language]] of [[Morobe Province]], [[Papua New Guinea]].

It is spoken in the single village of Nambom (also known as Banzain village) ({{coord|-6.433548|146.825565|type:city_region:PG|name=Banzain}}) in Gamiki ward, [[Wain-Erap Rural LLG]]. Ethnic Nafi people living in Popof village ({{coord|-6.438745|146.805971|type:city_region:PG|name=Popof}}) have since switched to speaking [[Nakama language|Nakama]], a Trans-New Guinea language. Intermarriages frequently occur between the two villages.<ref name="Holzknecht">{{cite book | first=Susanne | last=Holzknecht | title=The Markham Languages of Papua New Guinea | publisher=Pacific Linguistics| year=1989 | isbn=0-85883-394-8}}</ref>

